A||||28||FieroKyle||Overated/Underated Cars 1980-2000||||1||
Z||000000||FieroKyle||11-05-2001||11:08 PM||||What are you guys think? Heres my list.....<P>Overated:<BR>1. Mustang (In general, most are V-6s, 5.0, the 4.6 in the GT's)<BR>2. PT Cruiser <BR>3. Eclipse/Talon/Laser (not turbos)<BR>4. Celicas<BR>5. #$%^&*& (Did I say Vipers???? I meant rainx "wipers" ! REALLY!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P>Underated:<BR>1. Fieros of Course<BR>2. Buick Grand National (people forget how fast they really were)<BR>3. Impala SS<BR>4. Saab Turbo<BR>5. 90's Toronado<P>That what I could think of off the top of my head. I am sure theres more and may be a top ten of each would have been more apporiate. Anyways, you guys battle it out to you people think. I am sure some good cars will pop up that were forgotten.<P>No flaming intended. As far as it goes like just the general quality of the car, performance, looks, I guess some luxury, and may be a car is over hyped up, and another car has been had mislead information circle it and eventually killed it. (Like the Fiero) Also I am talking about these models in general, and not the suped up one that they came out with that they only made like under 1,000. I am just talking "in general".<P>There I have edited the list so, I think it came out better. <BR>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">        <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT<P><BR>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-06-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-07-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||falconhulk||11-06-2001||08:12 AM||||All dodges with the turbo 2 and turbo 3's.  Not even thought of as real sports cars.  They are way underrated.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gtsonly||11-06-2001||08:45 AM||||I don't think the Grand National and the Impala SS were under rated.  What is your definition of under Rated?  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero001_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||GodSend||11-06-2001||10:00 AM||||I don't think the Talons are overrated - Maybe the N/A's .. but the TSI AWD versions are hella fast stock!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And just so you know, they are half american!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000004||Svyn||11-06-2001||10:17 AM||||Overrated Viper? Apparently you have not had the pleasure of riding in one =). Under rated would have to be, Ford Thunderbird SC, and Pontiac GTP. <P>Both Eaton M90 supercharged from dealers showroom. SC was intercooled stock, was 25k, would pull a .85g in skidpad, 0-60 in 6.9 sec, 14.91 in the quarter. Don't forget this was a 4000 lb monster with driver. As far as the GTP, I don't have the numbers infront of me but I'm sure they are close to identical, minus being wrong wheel drive (front wheel), not having an intercooler, and weighing in 500 lb less. <A HREF="http://members.home.net/dcclark3/SCpage.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/dcclark3/SCpage.htm</A> <BR>My car, more information.<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Dale Clark<BR>86' Fiero SE<BR>99' Dodge Durango SLT+<BR>92' Ford ThunderBird SuperCoupe||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||11-06-2001||10:18 AM||||This all depends on definition.  Vipers overrated?  Um, I don't think so.  They do blow the doors off of most other stock sports cars in the world.  I'd also argue that the Eclipse trio and even the Mustang (flame suit on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) to a point aren't overrated either.  The Eclipse turbos as mentioned are awesome sport compacts.  Its such a shame Mitsu dumped the turbo motors.  The Mustang, especially in Cobra form, is running 0-60 in about 5.3 sec in Motor Trends latest test vs a Camaro, and far outhandles the Camaro.  Besides, most people will admit the Mustang is no sports car when it comes to handling, and that its also not the most refined machine.  It fulfills its mission well... to go fast.<P>My Over-rated:<P>The Celica GTS.  180 HP all above 6 grand and no low end torque.  Look at its acceleration numbers and its opbvious this thing can be a track star, but its not an ideal street machine.<P>Really, any car you have to spend a lot of money modifying to make a decent performer out of.  I am referring to the econoboxes, such as Civics.  If it makes a good performance car, it should be one right from the factory.  Nothin against anyone who improves a car thru mods, but I just don't understand trhowing lots of money into a car like a Civic to make it fast when the same dollars could make a better car to begin with a real screamer!<P>Under-rated<BR>I agree with the Impala SS.  Really die-hards love it, but a lot of people discount it as a big slow fancy Caprice.  <P>Also, the old Escort GT's with the Mazda MX-3 motors in them.  Those things were cheasy little hatchbacks, but they really flew!  They definately can take a Fiero V6 (trust me!)<P>Maybe the Fiero to a point, but its problems were always more of a bad quality reputation than a performance one.  So in that respect it definately is.  It was never the fastest car on the road, and compared to new cars today it is lacking a bit in HP.||||reg||1
Z||000006||The Fieromaster||11-06-2001||03:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GodSend:<BR><B>I don't think the Talons are overrated - Maybe the N/A's .. but the TSI AWD versions are hella fast stock!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And just so you know, they are half american!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Rob</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree... The DSM's (all the Eclipse, Talons, Lsers) were sooooo NOT overated! Yea, yea ok the rs's werent fast (1.8L) and the 2nd gen non turbos had the sh1tty Chrysler 2L BUT my 97 GSX (all wheel drive turbo) hauled azz!!!  Ask James (fieromaster88) 160mph like WOA!  Not to mention 5,ooorpm launches with NO spin! Talk about acceleration G's!  Oh yea... AWD doughnuts rule too!  in closing can i say this... 4 bangin eclipse vs Mustang GT... 4 banger wins everytime!  Just ask Chuck Mccabe about gettin whomped by a GSX!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">         <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">      <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                 <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000007||BlackStang95||11-06-2001||04:10 PM||||As kyle tries to start another flame thread, ill suffice to say it'd be extremely difficult to overrate Mustangs if you tried.  Ditto for Vipers.  The PT cruiser is a hell of a nice alternative to a wagon or suv in my opinion, and has anyone seen the hennessey one with 600 hp?  Sweet.  Fieros are generally well underrated, but are overrated on this board  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. The impala ss would be overrated in my book, they were pathetic for a vehicle with the SS badge.  T ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Spektrum-87GT||11-06-2001||05:42 PM||||what wierd twisted world do you live in?<P>1) the mustang gt is an affordable sports car that can also be a practical daily driver, cant say that about any other car, besides the z28(which in my opinion is overpriced and has a terrible build quality). if you're talking about the v6... its not overated at all, people seem to hate them.<BR>2) pt cruiser is a new design, so its gotten a lot of attention<BR>3) overated?!? people hate them! and the turbo versions were fast! non-turbo eclipses are overated, be specific next time!<BR>4) i'll give you the celica<BR>5) BAHASLDKFJA!!@#?!@?# no words for that one, overpriced *MAYBE* but definitly not overated.<P>1) fieros were definitly underated, some models more than others<BR>2) anyone who knows anything about fast cars knows about the grand national, i've never heard a bad thing about it. how can you say its underated?<BR>3) which year? the new ones? they're a joke<BR>4) 300m... its a chrysler... and a luxury car, kinda reminds me of the new yorker, its somewhat impossible to rate something like that.<BR>5) now the sho wasnt underated, just didnt sell good enough, not many soccer moms cared if their taurus was fast or not.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>What are you guys think? Heres my list.....<P>Overated:<BR>1. Mustang<BR>2. PT Cruiser<BR>3. Eclipse/Talon/Laser<BR>4. Celicas<BR>5. Vipers<P>Underated:<BR>1. Fieros of Course<BR>2. Buick Grand National<BR>3. Impala SS<BR>4. Chrysler 300M<BR>5. Taurus SHO (2nd Generation)<P>That what I could think of off the top of my head. I am sure theres more and may be a top ten of each would have been more apporiate. Anyways, you guys battle it out to you people think. I am sure some good cars will pop up that were forgotten.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Master_Sushi||11-06-2001||07:55 PM||||Impala SS was underated. It was the last of real american RWD cars! What can be better then a hot 350, 4 doors, big wheels stock, power everything, low to the ground, huge police edition brakes, lots of other options, AND REAR WHEEL DRIVE! This was the last true 4 door american muscle car!<P>Some may say the crown vic is simmilar, but they are complete garbage compared to the Impala SS. They are slow(SOHC <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ), handel like pigs, and they are made by ford.....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I think another very underrated car are turbo Saabs. I have driven a new 9-3 turbo. I also drive a 1987 9000 turbo daily. They are very fast, high quality (probably more then 1/2 the things in he car are German), very comfertable, and arn't hard to work on. Only thing I don't like is the "wrong wheel drive".<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000010||Mach10||11-06-2001||08:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>As kyle tries to start another flame thread, ill suffice to say it'd be extremely difficult to overrate Mustangs if you tried.  Ditto for Vipers.  The PT cruiser is a hell of a nice alternative to a wagon or suv in my opinion, and has anyone seen the hennessey one with 600 hp?  Sweet.  Fieros are generally well underrated, but are overrated on this board   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. The impala ss would be overrated in my book, they were pathetic for a vehicle with the SS badge.  T </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First of all, He was NOT NECESSARILY trying to flame you... Stop being so damn sensitive... Every time the word "Mustang" pops up, you make a scene about a new flame-war... It isn't.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>On the other hand the Mustang was never overrated... It was, and still is a Pony Car. RWD, v-8... The defining characteristics... Funny, it's the only one left, so it's doing SOMETHING right... (Fugly tho it be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P>As for the PT Cruiser: Lemme spell it for y'all: "A-S-S C-H-A-D-D-E-R"<BR>That was the most overrated car (except for maybe the NewDungBeetle) or this century... *shudder*<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000011||BlackStang95||11-06-2001||09:50 PM||||NEW DUNG BEETLE <P>first time ive heard that...funny stuff<BR>it gets my vote for most over-rated car ever.<BR>That and maybe the early-mid 90's standard corvettes...they really werent that quick for their nameplate.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroKyle||11-07-2001||12:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>now the sho wasnt underated, just didnt sell good enough, not many soccer moms cared if their taurus was fast or not.<P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 94's were sorta slow with the Yamaha, I leave unimpressed by them. I talking about the 2nd Gen, SHOs. They had a v-8, I forget what it was, but they were fast and mean. I though a Soccer Mom was a Mini Van???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I see a lot of guys with a SHO's.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Mach10||11-07-2001||12:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>NEW DUNG BEETLE <P>first time ive heard that...funny stuff<BR>it gets my vote for most over-rated car ever.<BR>That and maybe the early-mid 90's standard corvettes...they really werent that quick for their nameplate.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Love how VW touts their 'revolutionary' arch design... Yet my 5'2 GF bangs her head on the roof in the back seat,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I think they make GREAT igloos, though, if you bury them in enough snow  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
