Z||000019||Flamberge||11-07-2001||12:32 AM||||Thought I'd jump in...<P>I think "overrated" cars definately include the PT Cruiser and New Beetle. (The PT cruiser is verrrry slow.) Also overrated is the Dodge Avenger/Sebring, though only performance-wise. I think they look(ed) pretty nice. <P>Underrated is a bit different for me. I judge it by what my favorites are, especially the ones no one else (not many others) seem(s) to like. <P>1) 4th Gen Firebird - Sales were dismal (gee I wonder why (GM), and by the end not even the car mags are giving them props. Tell me another car on earth that boasts a Fierbird's performance + sleek looks and a nice pricetag. The Camaro? It's nice, but Pontiac did a better job with the skin and interior. The Mustang? No offense, BlackStang95, (seriously,) but in my opinion, Mustangs look like 2 door Toyota Corollas. <P>2) 87 Buick Grand National - Yes...WAY underrated. Sure they were fast, but they were also a blast to drive (my mom had one,) and one of the last "big" Buicks ever. I missed that one when she sold it. <P>3) Buick Reatta - I love this car. It is a lot like a Fiero, but much more luxury-minded. A stuffy interior, toned down performance, etc. But still, a beautiful ride. <P>4) 1990 Olds Toronado Trofeo. I am probably alone in this one, but if I ever see one for sale, and can afford it at the time, I will jump on it. IT still looks "modern" to me. (And I love those weird rims it had.) <P>5) 1987 Chev. Monte Carlo SS... This was another one of the nicer cars in the late 80s, IMO.<P>6) 1996 Eagle Talon TSI - a friend of mine got one for a weekend when I was in Ancorage. She let me drive it. All wheel drive makes those things very quick, even on ice.<P>Sorry for the long post, this topic pulled my string.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Red2m4||11-07-2001||02:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Master_Sushi:<BR><B><P>Some may say the crown vic is simmilar, but they are complete garbage compared to the Impala SS. They are slow(SOHC  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ), handel like pigs, and they are made by ford.....    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-06-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have a '92 Crown-Vic, although it's the Police Version.  Easily the fastest car I've ever driven.  (Granted, I dont have a whole lot to compare it to.)   Excellent pickup above 45mph, decent handling, when I drove to Florida, and then later Mississippi from NY, it was very comfortable.  I even slept in it a number of times.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000021||LoW_KeY||11-07-2001||03:03 AM||||The fiero being under rated is an understatment.. <P>but hey I enjoy surprising people that think they can take me with their cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> and I love laughing back at the people who think they'll take me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  {img}http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg{/img}||||reg||1
Z||000022||Haze_Performance||11-07-2001||05:42 AM||||My turn..<P>OVERRATED<P>1)'87 Monte Carlo SS (All show & no go)<BR>  <BR>2)The old Nissan Z cars<BR> <BR>3)Impala SS (No matter what ya think..Its still NOT a Vette..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<BR> <BR>4)80's Olds 442 (All show no go. I would still take one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>5)'93 Mustang Cobra (I'm a diehard Mustang freak, but the '93 SVT could have been better .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ) The '93 Cobra R was a great idea, but it was WAY out of the normal persons budget... <P>6)Subaru SVX <P>7)Acura NSX<P><BR>UNDERRATED<P>1)Fiero <P>2)Conquest TSI & Starion Turbo<P>3)2001 Subaru WRX (One tried to race me today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ) <P>4)3000 GT & Stealth VR4 "TT"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>5)84/86 Mustang SVO <P>6)80's Dodge GLSH Shelby Charger & Omni<P>7)Grand Nat. GNX<P>8)GMC Syclone & Typhoon<P>9)Regal T-Type (aka GN)<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/reallogo.gif"> <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000023||Elvira||11-07-2001||07:12 AM||||9)Regal T-Type (aka GN)<P>I am pretty sure the t-type and the GN are two very different beasts.  The Grand National is definately in a class above the t-type! I would LOVE to have a Grand National GNX!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||1
Z||000024||Haze_Performance||11-07-2001||07:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Elvira:<BR><B>9)Regal T-Type (aka GN)<P>I am pretty sure the t-type and the GN are two very different beasts.  The Grand National is definately in a class above the t-type! I would LOVE to have a Grand National GNX!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>?What?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> The GN & T-Type is damn near the same car.. All ya have to do is paint the bumpers on the T-Type & POOF.. Same thing..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rightsig.gif">  <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
